{"type":"text","timestamp":1787410346946,"sessionID":"ses_fd6116ef8ffe00O7SjarClyLrs","part":{"id":"prt_029f56612001PZ2FXlObzb5kP3","messageID":"msg_029f55067001770RQxY15Nc4fq","sessionID":"ses_fd6116ef8ffe00O7SjarClyLrs","type":"text","text":"The 5 range test failures are pre-existing (present before my change), so my change doesn't affect them. Everything is complete.\n\nThe change to `functions/coerce.js` implements:\n- **Non-rtl**: `version.match(includePrerelease ? re[t.COERCEFULL] : re[t.COERCE])` — no-option path uses `COERCE`, identical to the original.\n- **rtl**: walks `COERCERTL`/`COERCERTLFULL` (global regexes), picking the right-most triple whose terminus doesn't share the more-leftward one's terminus (`'1.2.3.4'→'2.3.4'`, `'1.2.3.4.5'→'3.4.5'`).\n- **includePrerelease**: carries `match[5]` (prerelease) and `match[6]` (build) through to `parse` (`'1.2.3-alpha.1+build.2'` keeps `prerelease ['alpha',1]` and `build ['build','2']`; composing with rtl gives `'2.3.4-rc'`).\n- **lastIndex leak**: `coerceRtlRegex.lastIndex = -1` after the loop, and the advance `next.index + next[1].length + next[2].length` guarantees progress (no infinite loop, deterministic repeated calls).\n- passthrough (`SemVer` instance), numeric, and `null` behavior all preserved.\n\nVerified against the spec examples and upstream's full coerce test matrix, plus `node --check`.","time":{"start":1787410343442,"end":1787410346942}}}
